# The .gitignore this unit breaks a repository with. Every line of it is defensible on its
# own, and together they cost a team an afternoon.
#
# It is not a straw man: `*.jar` is the single most common line in a Java .gitignore on the
# internet, because people paste it to keep build output out - and `target/` and `build/`
# already do that job. What `*.jar` adds is the wrapper.

*.jar
target/
